KG42.register("clusters-0df44fb2cc3e1e6252e9b063",{"id":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v142-d-K003","paper":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control","label":"Central air-conditioning supply configuration, demand aggregation, and clearing price return","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Central air-conditioning supply configuration, demand aggregation, and clearing price return","market_meaning":"Using the demand curve and the supply curve configured according to the service objective as inputs, aggregate demand and determine the intersection clearing price or the existing no-intersection return value; the electricity clearing price is also used to generate the lower-level water and air supply curves. The software chain provides the input-output interface for this central market process.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01","v141-a-M03"],"market_types":["LEM","DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"M01 describes the central system market behavior, and M03 describes the Market/Clearing interface of a central market of the same kind; they are complementary in the scope of behavior and implementation. The original labels LEM and DEM are both retained; the general clearing branch, the coverage mode of the reported worked example, and software algorithm equivalence remain unresolved.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Supply configuration, aggregation, and price return jointly complete the decision from curve inputs to the clearing price, and the transfer of the electricity price to lower-level supply has a clear process basis. Demand generation serves only as a shared interface, setpoint execution is handled by another Rule-Cluster, and the software chain is not counted separately as an independent clearing algorithm.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the electricity supply configuration under service conditions and the source of the water and air supply shapes and prices."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the clearing formulation for demand aggregation, supply input, and the intersection case."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the price-return branches under intersection and no-intersection conditions, and retains the conditions of the reported worked example."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R016","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Retains the input and implementation attribution of the central-market Market class and the Clearing function, and does not treat the interface declaration as proof of a complete algorithm."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R015","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Supplements the price output of the same software clearing interface; its mathematically unresolved status remains unchanged."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only references the demand-generation result as the input source for clearing; its generation mathematics is primarily the responsibility of the demand Rule-Cluster."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06"],"rationale":"Demand generation provides the demand curve for each central market, and aggregate clearing consumes the curve input of the corresponding market; this connection does not fill in the generation model omitted by R001."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e08"],"rationale":"The source explicitly states that each market participates in clearing through the corresponding supply curve, so supply configuration and clearing input are complementary; the branches for each commodity and DR service remain distinguished."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::V::clearing.local"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-E025"],"rationale":"Finding the intersection after aggregation and returning the intersection price jointly describe the clearing decision when an intersection exists; the wording in E025 regarding the number of curves remains ambiguous, so only a candidate functional connection is established."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E025","v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g02-E004"],"rationale":"Only at the commodity level of the electricity market clearing output is the clearing price mapped to the price input of the water and air supply curves; the prices of different markets are not treated as the same quantity, and no simultaneous-solving or loop algorithm is added on this basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R016","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001","v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C002","v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-E023","v141-b-g02-E024"],"rationale":"M01 describes central-market aggregation and clearing behavior, and M03 describes the interface through which the corresponding Market instance receives the demand and supply curves; the interface does not prove the aggregation location or equivalence of the complete algorithm."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R016","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R015","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E023","v141-b-g02-E024"],"rationale":"Table 5 lists the demand and supply curve inputs and the clearing price output as the contract of the Clearing function of the same Market class; the two Rule-Chains are complementary parts of the same software interface."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R016::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-E024"],"rationale":"Both reference the existing functional node for central-system demand input; the node display merge does not equate per-market curves, aggregated curves, and software arrays."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R016::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g02-E024"],"rationale":"Both reference the supply-input functional node; the respective scopes of commodity, service condition, and software representation are retained, and the supply functions are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R016::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R015::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-E025","v141-b-g02-E024"],"rationale":"Four places reference the same clearing functional node; this resolves only the functional-node display and does not claim that all M01 branches are proven to be implemented by the M03 interface."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R015::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E025","v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g02-E024"],"rationale":"All are references to the existing local price functional node; the clearing prices of different commodities and historical price statistics are not merged merely because the node is the same."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G01","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"E025 is worded as finding the intersection of two demand curves with a supply curve, whereas R006 explicitly aggregates demand horizontally first; the two input wordings cannot be automatically assumed to be completely equivalent.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E025","v141-b-g01-e06"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the original text of E025 and the Clearing input, clarify whether aggregated demand is used, whether additional curves exist, and where aggregation occurs; make an explicit revision by C."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G02","category":"scope_conflict","description":"R004 retains both the general no-intersection extremum return and the baseline-equivalent price and insufficient-flexibility minimum-price results of the reported worked example; its service scope and coverage priority are not uniformly specified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E026","ev-v141-b-g03-013","v141-b-g04-E01","v141-b-g04-E02","v141-b-g04-E03"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Separately confirm the conditions and coverage relationships of the general function, the demand-limiting worked example, and the load-following worked example; case results must not directly replace the general algorithm."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The supply capacity bound, the treatment when equal to the bound, the price domain, and the existence of extrema are not frozen; the intersection-set formulation in R006 does not specify multi-intersection selection or mathematical closure for no intersection.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-E026"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Supplement the curve domain, capacity boundary, extremum, and intersection-selection conditions supported by the source; if the original text does not define them, explicitly retain them as unresolved without inferring values or rules."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G04","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The two M03 Rule-Chains provide the software input-output and class attribution but do not freeze the complete Clearing algorithm; the mathematics of R015 remains unresolved and cannot be automatically repaired by borrowing the mathematical expression in R006.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R015","v141-c-R016"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C001","v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E023","v141-b-g02-E024"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If equivalence between implementation and market behavior needs to be verified, supplement the same-mechanism algorithm source and exception branches for M03, and handle the mathematics through explicit C revision; the current interface statement remains unchanged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G05","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Service-objective selection and power signals do not have independent approved objects, and all DR service inputs cannot be interpreted as price signals; the related service-objective proposal remains pending review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C007","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E030","v141-b-g02-E036","ev-v141-b-g03-001"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g02-P02","proposal-v141-b-g03-dr-service-objective"],"required_work":"Manually check the representation of the service-objective concept and the three types of service conditions, and retain the proposal's pending status; where extension is needed, handle it explicitly upstream."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G06","category":"unverified_source","description":"Both the market behavior and the software interface are assembled according to the candidate support catalog, and neither the M01 nor the M03 source has yet undergone an independent source audit.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R015","v141-c-R016"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-E025","v141-b-g02-E026","v141-b-g02-E023","v141-b-g02-E024"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently verify the market process, the original text of Clearing, and Tables 4–5, and separately confirm the source scope of the two mechanisms; this Rule-Cluster does not indicate that the algorithm or transcription has been approved."}]},"rule_refs":["46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R005","46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R006","46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R004","46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R016","46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R015","46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R001"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2922a59013d1b13e","COMP-3aa159734d0c0072","COMP-4c777fe6487767aa","COMP-80212c4bda48caf5","COMP-969c4da0a778db4f","COMP-98814ac540346a4b","COMP-ba9385174aa2f14e","COMP-c08cf41f234ed625","COMP-c1d0a111f9959db9","COMP-f25a5df437fc6d4f"]});
